ref 17592186045417] [17592186262496 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262496 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262496 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186261855 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262496 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "d63e23f4-baa1-51c3-b321-bbcaaaa933a6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262570 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186260037 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262570 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186260536 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262570 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186260758 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262570 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186261004 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262570 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186261846 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262570 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262570 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262570 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186260536 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262570 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "ffc75d90-c023-5fb9-a940-576505f511c9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262695 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186262461 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262695 #edb/ref 1069 "q-127046" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262695 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262695 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the parametric equations of the line that passes through the points $P(2,-5,4)$ and $Q(3,-2,2).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262695 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "198cf240-fd0a-5616-aefd-68b43c60564e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262695 #edb/ref 1074 "We need to find a direction vector that is parallel to the given line. We can use the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{OQ}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the vector equation of the line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}t \\\\ 3t \\\\ -2t\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2+t \\\\ -5+3t \\\\ 4-2t\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ And finally, the parametric equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=2+t \\\\ y &=-5+3t \\\\ z &=4-2t\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186262956 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186262494 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262956 #edb/ref 1069 "q-129158" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262956 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262956 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(-1,3,-4)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $6x+2y+3z=9.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262956 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "04f29aba-0bc5-533b-80be-91fd747ce6a1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262956 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's start by picking a point on the plane. To do that, we simply substitute some concrete values for $x$ and $y$ into the equation and solve for $z.$ Let's choose $x=1$ and $y=0$ (though it doesn't really matter what values we choose). Solving for $z,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6x+2y+3z & =9 \\\\ 6(1)+2(0)+3z & =9 \\\\ 3z & =3 \\\\ z & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the point $Q(1,0,1)$ which lies on the plane.\n\nComputing $\\overset{\\to }{PQ},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨1,0,1⟩-⟨-1,3,-4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,-3,5⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also need a normal vector to the plane. For any Cartesian equation of a plane $ax+by+cz=d,$ the normal vector is $n=⟨a,b,c⟩.$ So, for the plane $Π,$ we have $n=⟨6,2,3⟩.$ \n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|2\\cdot 6+(-3)\\cdot 2+5\\cdot 3|}{\\sqrt{{6}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{3}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|12-6+15|}{\\sqrt{36+4+9}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|21|}{\\sqrt{49}} \\\\  & =\\frac{21}{7} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186263250 #edb/ref 1080 "\\sqrt{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186263250 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186263250 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1a5cc75b-1aa1-5b30-9362-5f8752961da4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186263271 #edb/ref 1080 "\\sqrt{3}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186263271 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186263271 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1d98f894-779c-5822-84b3-85b9a53ad6b2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186263494 #edb/ref 1080 "i-2\\,j" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186263494 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186263494 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "371188b1-b7ec-57b7-b295-164f4505e38f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186263617 #edb/ref 1080 "2\\,i+j" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186263617 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186263617 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "468d5107-6a48-54fc-a274-623f490c7ae3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186263687 #edb/ref 1080 "2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186263687 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186263687 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4efb98a8-8a82-5879-9aee-9a09d6afe439" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186263707 #edb/ref 1080 "7\\,i+10\\,j" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186263707 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186263707 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "5224940d-41f5-5791-9620-631ff60b6036" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186263781 #edb/ref 1080 "4\\,i+j" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186263781