1 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186274905 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186272619 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186274905 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186272858 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186274905 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186272974 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186274905 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186273778 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186274905 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186274905 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186274905 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186272974 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186274905 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "9a0add09-f8b7-5571-85b6-3994fc452dcc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186274975 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186273114 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186274975 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186273178 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186274975 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186273907 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186274975 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186273933 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186274975 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186274228 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186274975 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186274975 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186274975 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186273933 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186274975 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "c2759a57-ee5d-532e-a24f-4499af67035f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275031 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186272434 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275031 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186272477 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275031 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186274120 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275031 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186274122 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275031 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186274543 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275031 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275031 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275031 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186272477 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275031 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "e1f7daa1-80eb-5764-a426-2110070d9e2b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275200 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186274975 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275200 #edb/ref 1069 "q-148669" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275200 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275200 #edb/ref 1071 "A local newspaper is sold by three distributors, $1,$ $2,$ and $3.$\n\n- Distributor $1$ gets $36%$ of the copies.\n\n- Distributor $2$ gets $23%$ of the copies, and $92%$ of those copies are sold.\n\n- Distributor $3$ gets $41%$ of the copies, and $95%$ of those copies are sold.\n\nIf $3%$ of all copies have some printing defect, $70%$ of defective copies are sold, and $2.5%$ of sold copies are defective, what is the probability that a randomly chosen copy bought by distributor $1$ is sold? Round your answer to $3$ decimal places." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275200 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "cbae7601-74f3-53d4-af26-b2c79a262289" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275200 #edb/ref 1074 "Let $R$ be the event that a copy has a printing defect, $S$ be the event that a copy is sold, and ${D}_{1},{D}_{2},{D}_{3}$ be the event that a copy is given to distributor $1,$ $2,$ or $3,$ respectively.\n\nLet's break down the information given in the problem statement:\n\n- From the bullet points, we have the following information:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & P({D}_{1})=0.36 \\\\  & P({D}_{2})=0.23 &  & P(S|{D}_{2})=0.92 \\\\  & P({D}_{3})=0.41 &  & P(S|{D}_{3})=0.95\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe disjoint union ${D}_{1}⊔{D}_{2}⊔{D}_{3}$ covers the entire sample space, and we have\n\n$$\nP({D}_{1})+P({D}_{2})+P({D}_{3})=0.36+0.23+0.41=1.\n$$\n\n- Since $3%$ of all copies has some printing defect, we have\n\n$$\nP(R)=0.03.\n$$\n\n- Since $70%$ of defective copies are sold, we have\n\n$$\nP(S|R)=0.7.\n$$\n\n- Since $2.5%$ of sold copies are defective, we have\n\n$$\nP(R|S)=0.025.\n$$\n\nWe want to find the probability that a randomly chosen copy bought by distributor $1$ is sold, which is represented as $P(S|{D}_{1}).$ \n\nUsing Bayes' theorem combined with the law of total probability, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(R|S) & =\\frac{P(S|R)P(R)}{P(S)} \\\\ P(R|S) & =\\frac{P(S|R)P(R)}{P(S|{D}_{1})P({D}_{1})+P(S|{D}_{2})P({D}_{2})+P(S|{D}_{3})P({D}_{3})} \\\\ 0.025 & =\\frac{(0.7)(0.03)}{P(S|{D}_{1})(0.36)+(0.92)(0.23)+(0.95)(0.41)} \\\\ 0.025 & =\\frac{0.021}{0.36P(S|{D}_{1})+0.6011}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this equation for $P(S|{D}_{1}),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0.025(0.36P(S|{D}_{1})+0.6011) & =0.021 \\\\ 0.36P(S|{D}_{1})+0.6011 & =\\frac{0.021}{0.025} \\\\ 0.36P(S|{D}_{1})+0.6011 & =\\frac{21}{25} \\\\ 0.36P(S|{D}_{1}) & =\\frac{21}{25}-0.6011 \\\\ P(S|{D}_{1}) & =\\frac{1}{0.36}(\\frac{21}{25}-0.6011) \\\\ P(S|{D}_{1}) & ≈0.664\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275619 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{5}{16}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275619 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275619 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1028c364-ce75-5836-a84c-a7b8c7109998" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275969 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{13}{24}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275969 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275969 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "37590d2d-228a-54b7-9ea1-ddb7e5c81f4d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186276293 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{13}{16}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186276293 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186276293 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "5b184341-4aed-5427-a6ea-c4f9d55ff988" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186276572 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{5}{8}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186276572 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186276572 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "78b9fe3f-4e98-52de-bbf1-6f4e65819078" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186277501 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{5}{24}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186277501 #edb/r